  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved labour migration governance frameworks and access to justice and services for migrant workers in line with international standards and best practices</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PHL 130 strengthens labour migration governance and protects the rights of Filipino migrant workers by advancing fair recruitment, decent work, and effective reintegration. 

Recent policies and laws passed or issued in 2024, and that have been supported, include: Magna Carta for Filipino Seafarers signed into law in September 2024; DMW Department Order (D.O.) 07 series of 2024 issued in October 2024 &#x2013; constituting the Technical Working Group for Filipino migrant fishers. 

DMW policies in the pipeline are a DO which will standardize the employment contract for Filipino migrant fishers regardless of flag state of the fishing vessel; DMW Sea-based Rules and Regulations governing the recruitment and employment of Filipino seafarers (including fishers) &#x2013; the Land-based Rules and Regulations was amended and issued in June 2023. DMW is revising the Sea-based Rules and Regulations. 

It supports the Labour and Employment Plan (LEP) 2023&#x2013;2028&#x2019;s priority on expanding access to employment and priority on inclusive social protection and contributes to the UN Sustainable Development Cooperation Framework (UN SDCF) 2024&#x2013;2028, by enhancing institutions that foster a rights-based and inclusive environment.

The initiative benefits migrant workers, their families, and institutions responsible for migration governance by expanding access to quality services and stronger protection mechanisms. 

The strategy is implemented with the Department of Migrant Workers, local governments, employers&#x2019; and workers&#x2019; organizations, and other national partners to ensure coherent policies, well-coordinated services, and stronger accountability in migration governance. By closing gaps in protection and reintegration, PHL 130 also enables migrant workers and their families to enjoy better access to rights, services, and opportunities while contributing to inclusive and sustainable development.</narrative>
  </description>
